  "id": "Compound::DB00475 - Gene::2566",
  "verbalization": "Chlordiazepoxide is shown to interact with Gabra1 and Gabra2, both of which are subunits of GABA receptors, and these receptors are implicated in the activity of Gabrg2. The evidence suggests that Chlordiazepoxide binds to these GABA receptor subunits, which in turn are involved in the function of Gabrg2. This implies a potential mechanism by which Chlordiazepoxide influences Gabrg2, possibly through modulation of GABA receptor activity. The overlapping involvement of Gabra1 and Gabra2 in the same pathway to Gabrg2 suggests a possible role for these subunits in the functional activation of Gabrg2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be clarified. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential link between Chlordiazepoxide and Gabrg2 through the GABA receptor system, emphasizing the importance of receptor subunit interactions in drug action.",
